1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,851
Joule heating is used everywhere.

2
00:00:02,851 --> 00:00:10,872
Heaters, irons and kettles use nichrome, an alloy with high resistivity and a high melting point.

3
00:00:10,872 --> 00:00:18,098
A fuse does the opposite job: a short tin lead wire that melts and breaks the circuit when the heating gets dangerous.

4
00:00:18,098 --> 00:00:26,171
And the Nepal Electricity Authority bills you in kilowatt hours: one kilowatt hour is three point six million joules.

